EXT. GLACIER CREVASSE - DAY

A blue slot in the ice, forty feet down, sheer walls glowing like glass. A rope runs up into white sky.

MARGUERITE VOSS, 40s, dangles at the bottom, crampons biting. TOBY KANE, 30s, hangs three feet above her, rope bunched in his gloves. At the lip, IZABELLA "IZZY" BRANDT, 30s, belays, braced against an ice axe.

IZZY
(shouting down)
Talk to me!

TOBY
Her leg's pinned!

MARGUERITE
I'm fine!

IZZY
Which of you is talking?

TOBY
Me! She means me!

The ice groans. A shelf cracks above them. Snow hisses down. Toby swings, grabs at the wall, kicks a foothold. Marguerite hugs the ice.

TOBY (CONT'D)
Cut her loose!

MARGUERITE ^
Don't cut me loose!

IZZY
Stop moving! Both of you!

The groan fades. Quiet. Snow dribbles. Marguerite's breath fogs. Toby peers down at her, then up at Izzy.

TOBY
(whispering)
She's stuck. I can reach her.

IZZY
(whispering)
How stuck?

MARGUERITE
Stuck like a stuck thing.

Toby laughs once, shakily. He lowers himself another foot. His hand finds her harness. The ice gives a final crack and holds.

IZZY
Pull!

Toby pulls. Marguerite's leg comes free with a spray of ice. She cries out, grabs his wrist, and they rise together, jerked up the wall in short grunting yanks.

At the lip, she hauls herself over first, then him. They collapse on the glacier, flat on their backs, staring at the sky.

IZZY (CONT'D)
(panting)
Never again.

MARGUERITE
(panting)
You say that every time.
